What:           /sys/class/mi_display/disp-DSI-0/disp_count_info
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Xiaomi Venus kernel maintainers
Description:
                Read-only diagnostics for the newer count-info ioctl. The
                original disp_count node retains its 15-field persistence ABI.

                system_build_version: bounded software build identifier.
                poweron_samples: completed OFF-to-ON measurements.
                poweron_last_ns, poweron_total_ns: monotonic time from the
                count-info ON request while the panel is OFF, to its first
                successful nonzero DCS backlight update. Repeated ON messages
                do not restart a pending measurement; OFF cancels it.
                commit_long: saturating sum of userspace frame-drop reports.
                tpidle_count: absolute counter last reported by SurfaceFlinger;
                repeated reports are not added, and a client restart may lower
                it. This is not a hardware touch interrupt count.
                fullscreen_aod_times: sessions with fullscreen requested and
                the panel in LP1/LP2. Duplicate state notifications are ignored.
                fullscreen_aod_active_ns, fullscreen_aod_longest_ns: monotonic
                durations including the currently open session.

                A different build identifier resets these software-generation
                diagnostics. Panel lifetime counters are unaffected. These
                diagnostics are not persisted across reboot.

What:           /sys/class/mi_display/disp-DSI-0/fullscreen_aod_status
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Xiaomi Venus kernel maintainers
Description:
                Read-only boolean requested by display feature 35. The same
                request sends display event 15 with a four-byte value and
                enables actual fullscreen-AOD session accounting. Venus keeps
                its existing panel-specific AOD and fingerprint commands.
